INTERPRETATION
============================================================================================================
Across these cases, cyclic pressure samples = 0/4284.
A pressure search returning DAGs should be read as a failed counterexample search but a successful certificate search: the obstruction has a topological order.

Proof-useful reframe:
  1. pressure sources are chargeable blockers;
  2. pressure sinks are exposed blocked runners;
  3. topological layers give an induction order;
  4. the first non-DAG sample would be the first serious disproof-like core.

The d1-descent column is not perfect, so the DAG is not merely sorting by nearest distance.  It is a real relation-level residue of the two-neighbor geometry.
